<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $23.19 bln on Oct 11.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $23.19 bln on Oct 11.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.19 billion on October 11, 1996, from $22.90 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Oct 11	Oct 4	  Oct 13</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     18,764	18,474	 18,865</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,410	 4,410	  4,405</p>
<p>    SDRs				    18	    18		8</p>
<p>    Total			     23,192	22,902	 23,278</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
